\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s1\sb360\sa80\sl252\slmult1 Introduction\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl252\slmult1\cf0\f1\fs20 People engage more deeply with guidance when it feels continuous, intentional, and aligned with their personal preferences. To strengthen trust, relevance, and emotional engagement across the Foundation for Talent Transformation platform, including both the web experience and the My Talents app, these requirements define enhancements to the AI Coach that support continuity, personalization, and multimodal interaction for self-development.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s2\sb160\sa80\sl252\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs28 Coaching Personas and Interaction Model\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl252\slmult1\cf0\f1\fs20 Both Registered Users and Guest Users may access the AI Coach. Guest Users (non-registered users) can start an AI Coach interaction without creating an account, enabling immediate access to guidance using text. To encourage deeper personalization and continuity, Guest Users will be prompted to sign up so the AI Coach can provide more tailored and persistent support.\par
To begin interacting with the AI Coach, a user is first asked to select the coaching style they wish to work with. This selection establishes the AI Coach\rquote s persona and frames how guidance is delivered throughout the interaction.\par
Each persona represents a distinct coaching style ({{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "\\l "}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf2\cf3\ul see Appendix A}}}}\f1\fs20 ) designed to support self-development and is defined by a fixed image, voice style, and descriptive coaching approach. These elements remain consistent to preserve the integrity and intent of each persona. Members may customize the persona\rquote s name and voice speaking speed to improve familiarity and personal resonance and may switch personas at any time to better align the AI Coach\rquote s coaching style with their current needs or context.\par
Once selected, the AI Coach will consistently present itself using the chosen persona, customized name, and configured voice speaking speed, and will conduct conversations in alignment with that persona\rquote s coaching style. If a Member asks the AI Coach for its name, it will respond using the customized name provided.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s2\sb160\sa80\sl252\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs28 Interaction Modes, Architecture, and Access Controls\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl252\slmult1\cf0\f1\fs20 The AI Coach supports two interaction modes:\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl252\slmult1 Text-based interactions, which allow users to engage in ongoing conversations without response-count limitations.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Voice-based interactions, which provide a more natural, conversational experience and are subject to daily response limits defined by user status and membership level.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl252\slmult1 To enable continuity across both interaction modes, the AI Coach maintains persistent conversational memory, allowing it to reference quiz results and prior conversations so interactions can continue over time rather than being treated as isolated exchanges. Persistent conversational memory is available only to registered users. All conversations are transcribed in real time to support accessibility, transparency, and continuity across both text-based and voice-based interactions.\par
Voice interactions also include enhanced behavioral controls, including real-time transcription, user interruption, and defined listening timeouts to ensure a predictable, respectful, and controlled audio experience.\par
From an architectural perspective, the AI Coach experience is delivered as a single, shared interface encapsulated within an iframe for web delivery and rendered within a WebView for native applications. This approach ensures consistent behavior and functionality across desktop browsers, mobile browsers, and the My Talents app, while minimizing divergence between web and app implementations.\par
These requirements apply to Guest Users, Free Members, and Paying Members. Guest Users do not have access to voice interactions. Free Members are subject to system-configured daily voice usage limits, as defined elsewhere. Paying Members are permitted up to a system-configurable number of AI Coach responses per day (initially set to 250), subject to fair-use policies and system protection controls. No new visual interface elements are introduced as part of this update; all changes are behavioral and architectural in nature.\par
The overarching goal of these enhancements is to provide an AI Coach that feels more human, consistent, and responsive over time, while maintaining clear boundaries around privacy, predictability, and user control.\par

