\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s2\sb160\sa80\sl252\slmult1\fs28 Terms used\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl252\slmult1\cf0\f1\fs20 Agent Personas are described below with the following terms:\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720 Coaching Style: The overall way the coach thinks, communicates, and guides conversations.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Core motive: The main goal or outcome that drives how the coach works.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Strengths: The coach\rquote s natural abilities that help create progress and results.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Limits: The common challenges that can appear when this coaching style is overused or not balanced.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}What works: The approaches and conditions that make this coaching style most effective.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Conversation style: The types of questions or phrases this coach uses to move the conversation forward.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}How to respond to this style: Guidance on how you can engage in a way that leads to the best outcomes.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}OpenAI agent guidance: Instructions that define how an AI coach should behave to match this coaching style.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Speed: The typical pace at which the coach prefers to think, decide, and act.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl252\slmult1\par

